<title>FRANCE: Alcatel wins GSM contract from SFR.</title>
<headline>Alcatel wins GSM contract from SFR.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel Telecom, a unit of Alcatel Alsthom, said on Wednesday it had won a contract worth over one billion francs to supply GSM equipment to French mobile telecommunications operator SFR in the 1996-1998 period.</p>
<p>Societe Francaise de Radiotelephone (SFR) is a unit of Generale des Eaux which counts Britain's Vodafone Plc among its shareholders.</p>
<p>The Global System for Mobile Communications (GSM) is a digital mobile telecommunications standard.</p>
</text>
